{"t":"2026-11-23T00:03:01.146Z","i":11,"do":"waitReply","expect":"a long answer streams in; it is readable, not cut off, and the buttons under it never cover the words","timeline":[{"at":97,"badges":[],"reactions":[],"thinking":true,"streaming":0},{"at":5641,"badges":[],"reactions":[],"thinking":false,"streaming":1},{"at":12058,"badges":[],"reactions":[],"thinking":false,"streaming":0}],"watchShots":[{"at":1734,"mark":1500,"shot":"21-long-wait-1.5s.png","badges":[],"reactions":[],"thinking":true,"streaming":0},{"at":3131,"mark":3000,"shot":"22-long-wait-3.0s.png","badges":[],"reactions":[],"thinking":true,"streaming":0},{"at":6010,"mark":6000,"shot":"23-long-wait-6.0s.png","badges":[],"reactions":[],"thinking":false,"streaming":1}],"firstReplyMs":5553,"newBubbles":1,"reactions":[],"ok":true,"duplicates":0,"lastReply":"Deep in the Sundarbans lived a tiger named Sheru who was tired of eating the same plain meal every day. One evening, a warm, spicy smell drifted over from a village wedding, and his nose followed it straight to a giant pot of biryani. He watched from the bushes as the old cook, Rahim Chacha, layered rice, saffron and fried onions with great care. Sheru decided that night that he would learn to make it himself.\n\nHis first tries were a disaster. He burnt the rice, used a whole fistful of chillies, and sneezed so hard that the monkeys fell out of their trees laughing. But Sheru kept going back to watch Rahim Chacha, learning to soak the rice, brown the onions slowly, and seal the pot with dough so the steam could do its magic. The hardest lesson for a tiger was patience: waiting while the pot sat on a low fire, without lifting the lid even once.\n\nAt last, one full-moon night, Sheru opened the pot and the whole forest went quiet. The rice was long and fluffy, the masala was just right, and the smell brought deer, monkeys and even the grumpy old crocodile to his clearing. Nobody ran away that night, because Sheru was too busy serving plates to chase anyone. From then on, the jungle knew him not as the fierce tiger, but as Sheru the biryani wala. 🐯\n\n5:32 AM","kit":[],"replyFaults":[],"ms":18194,"shot":"24-long.png"}
